   338	### 3.3 Pins 2 and 3 — and the answer to "does `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transfer?"
   339	
   340	The brief's standing instruction was not to assume TC-57's remedy transfers. It was measured.
   341	Both pins apply the **identical** contention — one external connection holding the WAL write
   342	lock — and differ only in which engine entry point is called.
   343	
   344	| pin | engine call | transaction behaviour | result | wall time |
   345	|---|---|---|---|---|
   346	| 2 | `Engine::transition` | `BEGIN DEFERRED`, read-then-upgrade (`lib.rs:8221`) | **`Err(Storage)`** | **0 ms** |
   347	| 3 | `Engine::write` | `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` (`lib.rs:18637`, the TC-57 fix) | **`Ok`** | **~935 ms** |
