   355	**So the answer is: yes, empirically, on this engine, at this baseline.** The remedy is not
   356	being transferred by analogy — the very same database, the very same contention, and the very
   357	same 5 000 ms default busy timeout produce a hard 0 ms failure for the DEFERRED promoting
   358	transaction and a successful ~935 ms wait for the `IMMEDIATE` one. That is as direct as this
   359	evidence gets without implementing anything.
